    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-01-2023-june/q2",
      "question": "<ol class=\"parts\"><li>Write <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2+4x-5\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(x+p)^2+q\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\"></span> are integers. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li><li>Hence use a standard integral from the formula book to find<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x^2+4x-5}}\\,\\mathrm dx\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Determine the mean value of the function<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x^2+4x-5}}\\qquad3\\leqslant x\\leqslant13\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>giving your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\\ln B\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> are constants in simplest form.</p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
