      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-01-2023-june/q5",
      "question": "<p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{x+5}{1}=\\dfrac{y+4}{-3}=\\dfrac{z-3}{5}\"></span></p><p>The plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_1\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2x+3y-2z=6\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Find the point of intersection of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_1\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\"></span> is the reflection of the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> in the plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_1\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>Show that a vector equation for the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\"></span> is<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r=\\begin{pmatrix}-7\\\\2\\\\-7\\end{pmatrix}+\\mu\\begin{pmatrix}10\\\\6\\\\2\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mu\"></span> is a scalar parameter.</p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li></ol><p>The plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_2\"></span> contains the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> and the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li>Determine a vector equation for the line of intersection of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_1\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_2\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>The plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_3\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r.\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\1\\\\a\\end{pmatrix}=b\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> are constants.</p><p>Given that the planes <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_1\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_2\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_3\"></span> form a sheaf,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"4\"><li>determine the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
