      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-01-2023-june/q6",
      "question": "<p>Water is flowing into and out of a large tank.</p><p>Initially the tank contains 10 litres of water.</p><p>The rate of flow of the water is modelled so that</p><ul><li>there are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\"></span> litres of water in the tank at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> minutes after the water begins to flow</li><li>water enters the tank at a rate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left(3-\\dfrac{4}{1+\\mathrm e^{0.8t}}\\right)\"></span> litres per minute</li><li>water leaves the tank at a rate proportional to the volume of water remaining in the tank</li></ul><p>Given that when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0\"></span> the volume of water in the tank is decreasing at a rate of 3 litres per minute, use the model to</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>show that the volume of water in the tank at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> satisfies<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\mathrm dV}{\\mathrm dt}=3-\\frac{4}{1+\\mathrm e^{0.8t}}-0.4V\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li>Determine <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(\\arctan\\mathrm e^{0.4t}\\right)\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>Hence, by solving the differential equation from part (a),</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li>determine an equation for the volume of water in the tank at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span>.<p>Give your answer in simplest form as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V=\\mathrm f(t)\"></span></p><span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li></ol><p>After 10 minutes, the volume of water in the tank was 8 litres.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"4\"><li>Evaluate the model in light of this information. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
      "steps": [
