    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-01-2023-june/q7",
      "question": "<p><strong>In this question you must show all stages of your working.</strong></p><p><strong>Solutions relying on calculator technology are not acceptable.</strong></p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Explain why, for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\in\\mathbb N\"></span><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{2n}(-1)^r\\mathrm f(r)=\\sum_{r=1}^{n}\\left(\\mathrm f(2r)-\\mathrm f(2r-1)\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>for any function <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(r)\"></span>.</p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Use the standard summation formulae to show that, for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\in\\mathbb N\"></span><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{2n}r\\left((-1)^r+2r\\right)^2=n(2n+1)\\left(8n^2+4n+5\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li><li>Hence evaluate<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=14}^{50}r\\left((-1)^r+2r\\right)^2\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol>",
